Article 4 The people's governments at all levels and the departments of the people's governments at or above the county level shall establish and improve the government information disclosure work system of their respective administrative organs, and designate an institution (hereinafter collectively referred to as the government information disclosure working institution) to be responsible for the daily work of government information disclosure of the administrative organ.
The specific functions of the government information disclosure working institution are:
(1) handling the government information disclosure matters of the administrative organ;
(2) maintaining and updating the government information disclosed by the administrative organ;
(3) organizing the compilation of the government information disclosure guide, the government information disclosure catalogue and the annual report on government information disclosure work of the administrative organ;
(4) organizing and conducting the review of government information to be disclosed;
(5) other functions related to government information disclosure as prescribed by the administrative organ.

Article 20 An administrative organ shall, in accordance with the provisions of Article 19 of these Regulations, proactively disclose the following government information of the administrative organ:
(1) administrative regulations, rules and normative documents;
(2) organ functions, institutional setup, office address, office hours, contact information, and the name of the person in charge;
(3) national economic and social development plans, special plans, regional plans and related policies;
(4) statistical information on national economic and social development;
(5) the basis, conditions, procedures and results of handling administrative licenses and other external management service matters;
(6) the basis, conditions and procedures for imposing administrative penalties and administrative compulsion, as well as administrative penalty decisions that the administrative organ considers to have a certain social impact;
(7) fiscal budget and final account information;
(8) items of administrative fees and their basis and standards;
(9) the catalogue, standards and implementation of government centralized procurement projects;
(10) the approval and implementation of major construction projects;
(11) policies, measures and their implementation regarding poverty alleviation, education, medical care, social security, promotion of employment, etc.;
(12) emergency plans, early warning information and response situations for public emergencies;
(13) supervision and inspection of environmental protection, public health, work safety, food and drugs, and product quality;
(14) positions, quotas, application conditions and other matters for the recruitment of civil servants, as well as the recruitment results;
(15) other government information that shall be proactively disclosed according to laws, regulations, rules and relevant state provisions.

Article 29 Where a citizen, legal person or other organization applies to access government information, the application shall be submitted to the government information disclosure working body of the administrative organ and shall be in written form, including letters and data messages; if written form is truly difficult, the applicant may submit an oral application, and the government information disclosure working body handling the application shall complete the government information disclosure application form on behalf of the applicant.
A government information disclosure application shall include the following content:
(1) the applicant's name or title, identity certification, and contact information;
(2) the name or document number of the government information applied for disclosure, or other characteristic descriptions facilitating the administrative organ's search;
(3) the form requirements for the government information applied for disclosure, including the method and channel of information access.

Article 31 The time of receipt of a government information disclosure application by the administrative organ shall be determined in accordance with the following provisions:
(1) Where the applicant submits the government information disclosure application in person, the date of submission shall be the date of receipt of the application;
(2) Where the applicant submits the government information disclosure application by mail, the date of signed receipt by the administrative organ shall be the date of receipt of the application; where the application is submitted by ordinary mail or other postal methods not requiring signed receipt, the government information disclosure working body shall confirm with the applicant on the day of receipt of the application, and the date of confirmation shall be the date of receipt of the application;
(3) Where the applicant submits the government information disclosure application via the internet channel or fax of the government information disclosure working body, the date confirmed by both parties shall be the date of receipt of the application.

Article 36 For a government information disclosure application, the administrative organ shall respond separately according to the following circumstances:
(1) Where the information applied for has already been proactively disclosed, inform the applicant of the method and channel for accessing such government information;
(2) Where the information applied for can be disclosed, provide the government information to the applicant, or inform the applicant of the method, channel and time for accessing such government information;
(3) Where the administrative organ decides not to disclose in accordance with the provisions of these Regulations, inform the applicant of the decision not to disclose and state the reasons;
(4) Where, after search, the information applied for does not exist, inform the applicant that the government information does not exist;
(5) Where the information applied for is not within the responsibility of this administrative organ for disclosure, inform the applicant and state the reasons; if the administrative organ responsible for disclosing the government information can be determined, inform the applicant of the name and contact information of such administrative organ;
(6) Where the administrative organ has already responded to the government information disclosure application submitted by the applicant and the applicant repeatedly applies for disclosure of the same government information, inform the applicant that the application shall not be processed repeatedly;
(7) Where the information applied for falls under such information as commercial registration and real estate registration materials, and the relevant laws or administrative regulations have special provisions on accessing such information, inform the applicant to handle the matter in accordance with the provisions of the relevant laws and administrative regulations.

Article 50 The annual report on government information disclosure work shall include the following contents:
(1) the circumstances of the administrative organ's proactive disclosure of government information;
(2) the circumstances of the administrative organ's receipt and handling of government information disclosure applications;
(3) the circumstances of applications for administrative reconsideration and the filing of administrative actions due to government information disclosure work;
(4) the main problems in government information disclosure work and the improvement situation; the annual report on government information disclosure work of people's governments at all levels shall also include the results of work assessment, social appraisal, and accountability;
(5) other matters that need to be reported.
The competent department of national government information disclosure work shall publish a unified format for the annual report on government information disclosure work and shall update it as appropriate.

Article 53 If an administrative organ violates the provisions of these Regulations and falls under any of the following circumstances, the administrative organ at the next higher level shall order it to make corrections; if the circumstances are serious, the responsible leaders and directly responsible personnel shall be given sanctions according to law; if a crime is constituted, criminal liability shall be investigated according to law:
(1) failing to perform the function of government information disclosure according to law;
(2) failing to timely update the disclosed government information contents, the government information disclosure guide, and the government information disclosure catalog;
(3) other circumstances that violate the provisions of these Regulations.
